</pre>
```
:::

:::
:::


Use a tuple default, or `None` and build the list inside.

### `fold()` takes its dtype from the accumulator {#sec-prog-fold-dtype}

`pl.lit(0)` is `Int32`, and `pl.fold()` casts its result to the
accumulator's dtype: floats are truncated, `Int32` overflow becomes null, no
warning:

::: {#b2236134 .cell execution_count=25}
``` {.python .cell-code}
penguins_df.select(
    folded=pl.fold(pl.lit(0), operator.add, cs.ends_with("_mm")),
    horizontal=pl.sum_horizontal(cs.ends_with("_mm")),
).head(2)
```

::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=25}
```{=html}
<div><style>
.dataframe > thead > tr,
.dataframe > tbody > tr {
  text-align: right;
  white-space: pre-wrap;
}
</style>
<small>shape: (2, 2)</small><table border="1" class="dataframe"><thead><tr><th>folded</th><th>horizontal</th></tr><tr><td>i32</td><td>f64</td></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>238</td><td>238.8</td></tr><tr><td>242</td><td>242.9</td></tr></tbody></table></div>
```
